WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.240
Assessment is a clinical argument.

2
00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.120
Week one puts clinical reasoning at the center: gather information from

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:11.160
several sources, interpret it critically, and decide what the evidence supports.

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.700
The seven-stage framework begins with referral and review.

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.320
History and interview come next, then observation, assessment, analysis,

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.700
diagnosis and recommendations, and the report and results conference.

7
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.540
A test score is evidence within that process.

8
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.570
It cannot replace the process.

9
00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:32.340
The slide you flagged for Test One names four features.

10
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.480
Be thorough.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.640
Use a variety of assessment methods.

12
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.540
Use evidence-based approaches.

13
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.940
Tailor the assessment to the individual.

14
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.660
Keep their explanations paired correctly: valid and reliable methods belong to evidence

15
00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:51.000
based; age, skill level and ethnocultural background belong to individual tailoring.

16
00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:54.780
Evidence-based practice integrates research and client data, clinical

17
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.540
expertise, and the client or caregiver perspective.

18
00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:03.100
Internal evidence comes from your client; external evidence comes from scientific research.

19
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.760
The four steps are frame the question, gather evidence,

20
00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.380
assess the evidence, and make the clinical decision.

21
00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.160
Assessment must also remain within your professional competence.

22
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.680
The assigned videos extend this reasoning to test selection.

23
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:24.460
Check purpose, diagnostic accuracy, normative representation, relevant skills, reliability, and sufficiency.

24
00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:26.560
A screening instrument does not become a

25
00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.260
diagnostic instrument because it is convenient.

26
00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.120
Sensitivity and specificity apply to the particular target disorder studied.

27
00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:38.180
If a test score conflicts with everyday communication,

28
00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.713
gather converging evidence and document the limits.
